From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:06:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/27] rnd/sov-002: keep node-refused blocks; an NTA refusal
 is invalid now

A bad-nta-* verdict judges the coinbase the miner hashed, so the block can never
become valid: release its books at once, as for high-hash (it is not the
gateway's template fault). Prime also keeps the bytes of any block its node
refuses in data-dir/rejected-blocks/<hash>.hex: an invalid block is never
relayed, and the demo replays it to the other enforcing nodes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
